<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-Swedbank '96 profit 31 pct up.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Swedbank '96 profit 31 pct up.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Swedbank is expected to post a profit after credit losses of 4.99 billion crowns for the full year 1996, according to a Reuters poll of 14 analysts on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Forecasts range between 4.45 billion crowns and 5.19 billion.</p>
<p>In 1995 the bank reported an operating profit of 4.31 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Swedbank posted a profit of 3.82 billion crowns in the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>For 1996, credit losses are expected to land at 1.75 billion crowns, which makes analysts expect a profit before credit losses of 6.7 billion crowns.</p>
<p>When releasing nine-month earnings, the bank proposed a dividend of five crowns for the full-year 1996.</p>
<p>Swedbank will release 1996 figures on February 19.</p>
<p>Analysts polled came from Aros, BZW, Carnegie, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Enskilda, Fiba, Handelsbanken, J.P. Morgan, James Capel, Kleinwort Benson, Morgan Stanley, Penser, Swedbank and Ohman.</p>
